  "answer": "The *indent* argument controls pretty‑printing of the JSON output. If you pass a non‑negative integer, each level of nesting is indented by that many spaces; if you pass a string (e.g., \"\\t\"), that string is used for each indentation level. An *indent* of 0, a negative number, or the empty string results in only newlines being inserted. The default value is ``None``, which produces the most compact representation (no extra whitespace).",
